      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11087546::chunk::000::abstract::0f6f5ee9c1"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting alloy has a lamellar or mixed-phase microstructure and limited fracture resistance.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11087546::chunk::000::abstract::0f6f5ee9c1"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "HPHT treatment induces a hierarchically patterned microstructure with coherent interfaces in a eutectic HEA.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11087546::chunk::000::abstract::0f6f5ee9c1"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Controlled cooling after a non-melting HPHT treatment stabilizes newly formed phases and coherent interfaces.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "HPHT should be effective in eutectic or multiphase HEAs whose chemistry permits coherent precipitates or lamellae.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11087546::chunk::000::abstract::0f6f5ee9c1"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "HPHT may be less effective for single-phase HEAs or compositions that are too brittle or incompatible with the required transformations.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The hierarchical structure may consist of alternating soft FCC and hard BCC or intermetallic regions.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Coherent interfaces impede dislocation motion and thereby increase strength.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11087546::chunk::000::abstract::0f6f5ee9c1"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Impeded dislocation motion at coherent interfaces increases Young's modulus.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The HPHT-induced microstructure relieves stress concentrations at interfaces.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11087546::chunk::000::abstract::0f6f5ee9c1"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relieving interfacial stress concentrations arrests interfacial cracking.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11087546::chunk::000::abstract::0f6f5ee9c1"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The hierarchical microstructure activates multiple deformation mechanisms, including dislocation activity, microbands, and deformation twinning.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11087546::chunk::000::abstract::0f6f5ee9c1"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Activation of multiple deformation mechanisms helps overcome the conventional strength-ductility trade-off.",
